From 15cceb4df8ade7008f3f47a537e409a7ed4c9690 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:08:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] turnip (Doris): time every GPU operation for 1 s of every 30
 (fixed: turnip's tracepoints are markers)

Apex Doris 4's operation timing wrote nothing: it only looked at events marked as begin/end
ranges, and turnip's tracepoints are all plain markers. The Doris hook in u_trace now gets every
event and pairs start_/end_ names itself. Sampling is 1 s of every 30 (about 30 frames), so the
cost outside it is nil; every 30 s apex_doris.txt gets the GPU time per frame split into render
passes (5+ draws, 1-4, none), uploads, downloads, image copies, blits, clears, buffer copies,
compute, LRZ and the time between operations, what inside render passes takes the time, and the
20 biggest groups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
